.TH LAYERS 2
.SH NAME
layers \- what is drawn over a video, stacked by the name space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "layers.m";
layers := load Layers Layers->PATH;
Mark, Stack: import layers;

Box, Line, Text, Point: con iota;

init:  fn(): string;
parse: fn(line: string): (int, ref Mark);

Stack.watch: fn(dir: string): ref Stack;
Stack.due:   fn(s: self ref Stack, frame: int): list of ref Mark;
Stack.stop:  fn(s: self ref Stack);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A video feed's
.B layer
directory holds what is drawn over it, a file a layer.
The name space stacks them:
the layers are in the order the directory's union lists them, the first
at the bottom, so
.B bind -b
puts a directory's layers underneath,
.B bind -a
on top, and
.B unmount
takes them away.
Each viewer draws the stack its own name space has.
.PP
A layer is text, a record a line, each
.IB attr = value\fR:
.IP
.EX
frame=1234 box x0=320 y0=180 x1=384 y1=320 label=person
frame=1234 line x0=10 y0=400 x1=630 y1=400 colour=accent
frame=1234 text x=10 y=10 label='3 people'
frame=1234 point x=200 y=150
frame=* box x0=100 y0=80 x1=500 y1=400 label=door
frame=1235
.EE
.PP
Coordinates are the frame's pixels.
.B frame=*
is every frame; a frame's key alone is nothing on that frame.
On frame
.I F
a layer shows its records for the newest frame up to
.IR F ,
and its
.B frame=*
records.
A record with
.B x0 y0 x1 y1
and no kind is a box, labelled by
.BR label= ,
or else by
.B class=
and
.BR score= ,
so the detections of
.IR visionfs (4)
are a layer as they come.
.B colour=
is a theme's name
.RB ( accent ,
.BR red ,
\&...) or
.IR rrggbb ;
a record with none is drawn in the accent, or, a detection's, in its
class's colour: one of the theme's eight categorical colours
.RB ( pie0
to
.BR pie7 ,
as charts use), chosen by a hash of the class's name, so a class is the
same colour in every frame, viewer and run.
Attributes it does not know are ignored, and a line that is no record is
skipped.
.PP
A file that ends is read once and kept; one rewritten is read again.
.IR Layerfs (4),
union-mounted with create over a
.B layer
directory, makes any file written there a layer.
A file that waits (a session's detections, a pipe) is read as it comes,
a frame's records a read.
.PP
.B Stack.watch
follows the layer directory
.IR dir ,
listing it every half second for layers bound and unmounted, with a
process reading each layer.
.B Stack.due
gives the marks due on
.IR frame ,
bottom layer first.
.B Stack.stop
stops its processes.
.B Parse
reads a line as
.RI ( frame ,\  mark ):
.I frame
is \-1 for
.B frame=*
and \-2 for a line that is no record;
.I mark
is nil for a frame's key alone.
.SH EXAMPLES
Detections over the camera, then a hand-drawn line above them:
.IP
.EX
bind -a /mnt/vision/1/layer /mnt/video/0/layer
echo 'frame=* line x0=0 y0=300 x1=640 y1=300' > /tmp/horizon/h
bind -a /tmp/horizon /mnt/video/0/layer
.EE
